  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting FoRB between Palestinian Christians and Muslims and Israeli Jews through reconciliation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the proposed project, Musalaha aims to educate, engage and equip Muslim and Christian Palestinains from the West Bank and Muslim and Chistians Palestinian Citizens of Israel and Jewish Israelis in FoRB. While providing this FoRB education, Musalaha relies upon its Curriculum for Reconciliation to form relationships across faiths, etnicities and borders. Once Israelis and Palestinians have an increased empathy, understanding and humanity for their &quot;other&quot; neighbors in the Land, Musalaha equips and engages all individuals to non-violently co-resist oppressive and discriminatory structures and dehumanizing narratives and to advocate for an equal, inclusive justice for all. Promoting FoRB through grassroots outreaches in Muslim and Christian communities in the West Bank, and in Muslim, Christian and Jewish communities in Central Israel is an integral part of this co-resistance.</narrative>
  </description>
